  "body": "Currently, https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#fragment-state requires that we percent-encode characters in a URL's fragment using the [C0 control percent-encode set](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#c0-control-percent-encode-set). Firefox currently encodes more than that, which I think actually makes a good deal of sense.\r\n\r\nHow would y'all feel about shifting fragment state encoding to match query state? That is, encoding \"less than 0x21 (!), greater than 0x7E (~), or is 0x22 (\"), 0x23 (#), 0x3C (<), or 0x3E (>)\"?",
